\pard\sa140\b\fs28\f0 7. Important Business Rules\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - Only authenticated `patient` accounts can use the self-booking flow.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - Appointment times are generated from clinic config (`config/clinic.php`).\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - Dentist availability depends on:\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 - dentist account being active\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 - selected day matching `schedule_days`\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 - no non-cancelled appointment conflict for the same slot\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - Staff-created appointments default to `pending`.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - Patient self-booked appointments default to `scheduled`.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - Cancelled appointments are excluded from availability checks.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - Patient sensitive profile changes (`email`, `phone`, `medical_alerts`) use approval requests instead of direct updates.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - Treatment records are limited to the dentist who owns them.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - Dentist patient access is constrained to patients with appointments under that dentist.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - Notifications are role/user-specific and access-controlled.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - Audit logging is used across major create/update/cancel/export/backup actions.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa140\b\fs28\f0 8. End-to-End Data Flows\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa140\b\fs28\f0 8.1 New patient landing inquiry flow\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Purpose\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 Captures an unverified prospective patient from the landing page and routes the request to staff for validation.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Sequence\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 1. User fills out the inquiry form on `Home.jsx`.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 2. Frontend posts to `POST /inquiries`.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 3. `LandingInquiryController@store` validates input.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 4. System checks whether `patient_inquiries` table exists.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 5. System optionally matches the inquiry email to an existing user.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 6. `PatientInquiry` record is created with status `pending_verification`.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 7. All active staff users receive database notifications.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 8. Audit log entry is created.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 9. User is redirected back to home with a success flash message.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Mermaid sequence\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa0\fs18\f1 sequenceDiagram\par
\pard\sa0\fs18\f1     participant Visitor\par
\pard\sa0\fs18\f1     participant HomePage\par
\pard\sa0\fs18\f1     participant LandingInquiryController\par
\pard\sa0\fs18\f1     participant PatientInquiry\par
\pard\sa0\fs18\f1     participant Notification\par
\pard\sa0\fs18\f1     participant AuditLog\par
\pard\sa0\fs18\f1     participant StaffUsers\par
\pard\sa0\fs18\f1 \par
\pard\sa0\fs18\f1     Visitor->>HomePage: Submit inquiry form\par
\pard\sa0\fs18\f1     HomePage->>LandingInquiryController: POST /inquiries\par
\pard\sa0\fs18\f1     LandingInquiryController->>PatientInquiry: Create pending_verification inquiry\par
\pard\sa0\fs18\f1     LandingInquiryController->>Notification: Create notification for each active staff user\par
\pard\sa0\fs18\f1     Notification-->>StaffUsers: New inquiry appears in staff portal\par
\pard\sa0\fs18\f1     LandingInquiryController->>AuditLog: Log inquiry submission\par
\pard\sa0\fs18\f1     LandingInquiryController-->>HomePage: Redirect with success message\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa140\b\fs28\f0 8.2 Inquiry conversion to registered patient flow\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Purpose\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 Allows staff to verify landing-page submissions and convert them into full patient records and patient portal accounts.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Sequence\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 1. Staff opens inquiry list.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 2. Staff opens conversion page for a specific inquiry.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 3. Staff submits verified patient details and optional temporary password.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 4. System finds or creates a `User` with role `patient`.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 5. System updates or creates the related `Patient`.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 6. Inquiry status becomes `converted`.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 7. Notifications for that inquiry are marked read.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 8. Audit log entry is created.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Output artifacts\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - `users` row\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - `patients` row\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - updated `patient_inquiries` row\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - `audit_logs` row\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa140\b\fs28\f0 8.3 Patient self-booking flow\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Purpose\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 Allows only logged-in patient users to book their own appointments.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Sequence\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 1. Patient opens `/appointments/book`.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 2. System confirms authenticated role is `patient`.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 3. UI loads:\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 - active dentists\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 - clinic time slots\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 - available booking days\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 - existing non-cancelled appointments\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 4. UI requests available times for a chosen dentist/date.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 5. Backend checks:\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 - dentist active state\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 - dentist schedule day\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 - slot conflict\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 6. Patient submits booking form.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 7. Backend resolves or creates linked patient profile.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 8. Appointment is created with status `scheduled`.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 9. Audit log entry is created.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 10. User is redirected to confirmation page.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
