\pard\sa140\b\fs28\f0 8.4 Staff-managed appointment flow\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Purpose\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 Allows staff to create, edit, remind, export, and cancel appointments for clinic operations.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Create appointment sequence\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 1. Staff selects patient, dentist, date, time, type.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 2. Controller validates the request.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 3. Availability is checked through `AppointmentAvailability`.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 4. Appointment is created with status `pending`.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 5. Email is sent to dentist.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 6. Optional email is sent to patient.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 7. In-app notification is created for dentist.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 8. In-app notification is created for patient.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 9. Audit log entry is created.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Reminder sequence\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 1. Staff triggers reminder.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 2. `SendAppointmentReminderJob::dispatchSync` runs immediately.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 3. Patient receives in-app notification.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 4. Audit log entry is created.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Update/cancel sequence\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - update changes schedule details after conflict validation\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - cancel marks status as `cancelled`\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - exports generate PDF or Excel files\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa140\b\fs28\f0 8.5 Dentist cancellation flow\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Purpose\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 Lets a dentist cancel one of their own future appointments.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Sequence\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 1. Dentist opens own appointment calendar.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 2. Dentist cancels a future appointment.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 3. System verifies the appointment belongs to that dentist.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 4. Appointment status becomes `cancelled`.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 5. Patient receives cancellation email.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 6. Patient receives in-app cancellation notification.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 7. All staff users receive in-app cancellation notifications.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 8. Audit log entry is created.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa140\b\fs28\f0 8.6 Treatment record flow\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Purpose\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 Lets dentists document clinical visits and attach supporting files.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Sequence\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 1. Dentist chooses a patient from patients previously seen by that dentist.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 2. Dentist submits visit date, procedures, notes, prescription, and tooth data.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 3. System optionally links the treatment record to a same-day appointment.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 4. Treatment record is stored inside a database transaction.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 5. Uploaded files are stored on the `public` disk.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 6. Attachment metadata is saved in `treatment_record_attachments`.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 7. Audit log entry is created.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Data produced\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - treatment record row\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - zero or more attachment rows\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - files under `storage/app/public/treatment-records/...`\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa140\b\fs28\f0 8.7 Patient profile change request flow\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Purpose\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 Separates direct profile edits from approval-required sensitive changes.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Direct fields\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - first name\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - last name\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - date of birth\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - gender\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - address\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Requested fields\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - email\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - phone\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - medical alerts\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Sequence for requested fields\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 1. Patient submits a request with field/value.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 2. Backend validates allowed field and format.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 3. `ProfileChangeRequest` is created with status `pending`.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 4. Audit log entry is created.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 5. Request appears in patient history for tracking.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa140\b\fs28\f0 8.8 Reporting and export flow\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Purpose\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 Generates operational and analytical outputs for admin and staff.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Data sources\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - `appointments`\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - `patients`\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - `treatment_records`\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Processing\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 `App\\Support\\ReportData` computes:\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - appointments by day\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - daily summary\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - patient growth by month\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - procedure distribution\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - revenue estimate\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - appointments table\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Outputs\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - admin dashboard charts\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - admin reports page\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - staff reports page\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - PDF export\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - Excel export\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa140\b\fs28\f0 8.9 Backup and restore flow\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Purpose\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 Provides SQLite file-level backup management through the admin module.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Sequence\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 1. Admin creates backup.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 2. Database file `database/database.sqlite` is copied to `storage/app/backups`.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 3. Backup metadata is shown in backup UI.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 4. Admin can download, restore, or delete by validated filename pattern.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 5. All operations are audit logged.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa140\b\fs28\f0 9. Cross-Cutting System Behaviors\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa140\b\fs28\f0 9.1 Authentication and access control\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - Laravel auth routes handle login, registration, password reset, and email verification.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - New self-registered users are created as `patient`.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - `/dashboard` redirects authenticated users to the correct role dashboard.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - `CheckRole` middleware gates route groups.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa140\b\fs28\f0 9.2 Inertia shared state\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 Every Inertia page can receive:\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - authenticated user summary\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - unread notification count for dentist/staff/patient roles\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - flash messages\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 This is supplied by `HandleInertiaRequests`.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa140\b\fs28\f0 9.3 Notifications\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 Notifications are database records, not Laravel broadcast notifications.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 Common notification types include:\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - `patient_inquiry_submitted`\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - `appointment_booked`\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - `appointment_reminder`\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - `appointment_confirmed`\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - `appointment_cancelled`\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa140\b\fs28\f0 9.4 Audit logging\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 `AuditLog::log()` centralizes action logging with:\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - user id\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - action\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - module\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - description\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - IP address\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 This supports accountability and admin review.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa140\b\fs28\f0 9.5 Queue jobs and observers\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 `AppointmentObserver` is registered in `AppServiceProvider`.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Created appointment\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - schedules `SendAppointmentReminderJob` for 24 hours before the visit at 9:00 AM\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Updated appointment\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - if status changes to `confirmed`, dispatches `NotifyAppointmentConfirmedJob`\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 This means some appointment side effects are asynchronous and depend on a running queue worker.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa140\b\fs28\f0 9.6 Config-driven scheduling\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 `config/clinic.php` drives:\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - clinic opening hours\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - slot interval\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - allowed treatment procedure list\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 `ClinicHelper::generateTimeSlots()` uses this config for booking UIs.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
