\pard\sa140\b\fs28\f0 13. Risks, Constraints, and Documentation Notes\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - The backup flow is SQLite-file based, so the current backup documentation should describe SQLite deployment assumptions.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - Notification delivery is database-based; real-time push/websocket behavior is not implemented in this codebase.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - Reminder and confirmation automation rely on queue workers actually running.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - Some feature availability is migration-sensitive:\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 - `patient_inquiries`\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 - `user_settings`\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - Reports currently estimate revenue with a fixed multiplier rather than a billing/invoice model.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22\f0 - There is no visible admin approval workflow yet for processing `ProfileChangeRequest`; the request capture exists, but approval handling is not exposed in the route map reviewed here.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa140\b\fs28\f0 14. Documentation Boilerplate You Can Reuse\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 One-sentence system description\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 The Dental Clinic Management System is a role-based clinic operations platform that manages patient intake, appointments, treatment records, notifications, reporting, and administrative controls through a Laravel and React Inertia architecture.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Short architecture summary\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 The application uses Laravel as the backend application layer and React with Inertia.js as the frontend presentation layer. Business logic is organized by role-specific controllers, persisted through Eloquent models, and extended with queue jobs, email notifications, exports, audit logs, and file-based backup handling.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\b\fs24\f0 Short data flow summary\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 Most workflows begin with a user action in an Inertia React page, pass through a Laravel controller for validation and business rules, update one or more relational records, and then optionally trigger notifications, emails, queue jobs, exports, or audit log entries before returning an Inertia response or redirect.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
\pard\sa120\fs22\f0 \par
